{
  "title": "50: Qaaf ق",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-beneficent, the All-merciful\nقٓۚ وَالْقُرْاٰنِ الْمَجِيْدِۚ‏(1)\nQAA WAL QURAANIL AL-MAJEEDE.\nQaf (Q); By the Glorious Quran\nبَلْ عَجِبُوْۤا اَنْ جَآءَهُمْ مُّنْذِرٌ مِّنْهُمْ فَقَالَ الْكٰفِرُوْنَ هٰذَا شَىْءٌ عَجِيْبٌ‌ۚ‏(2)\nBAL A’AJEBOOA AN JAAA-AHUM MMUNZERUN MINHUM FAQAALA KAAFEROON HAAZAA SHAY-UN A’AJEEBUN.\nNay! wonder they that hath come unto them a warner from among themselves, so say the disbelievers: “This is a wonderful thing!\nءَاِذَا مِتْنَا وَكُنَّا تُرَابًا ‌ۚ ذٰ لِكَ رَجْعٌ ۢ بَعِيْدٌ‏(3)\nA-EZAA MITNAA KUNNAA TORAABANW ZAA LEKA RAJA’UN BAE’EEDUN.\nWhat! when we are dead and have become dust (shall we return)? That is a return far (from the truth)\nقَدْ عَلِمْنَا مَا تَنْقُصُ الْاَرْضُ مِنْهُمْ‌ۚ وَعِنْدَنَا كِتٰبٌ حَفِيْظٌ‏(4)\nQAD A’LIMNAA MAA TANQUSU ARZO MINHUM WAE’ENDANAA KETAABUM HAFEEZUN.\nIndeed, know We what reduceth the earth of them, with Us is a written record that secureth.\nبَلْ كَذَّبُوْا بِالْحَقِّ لَمَّا جَآءَهُمْ فَهُمْ فِىْۤ اَمْرٍ مَّرِيْجٍ‏(5)\nBAL KAZZABOO BIL-HAQQE LAMMAA JAAA-AHUM FAHUM FEE AMRIN MMAREEJIN.\nNay! they belied the truth when it came unto them, so they are in a confused state.\nاَ فَلَمْ يَنْظُرُوْۤا اِلَى السَّمَآءِ فَوْقَهُمْ كَيْفَ بَنَيْنٰهَا وَزَ يَّنّٰهَا وَمَا لَهَا مِنْ فُرُوْجٍ‏(6)\nA’ZAABAN FALAM YANZUROOA ELAL SAMAAA-E FAWQAHUM KAYFA BANAYNAAHAA WAZA YYANNAAHAA WA MAA LAHAA MIN FUROOJIN.\nWhat! See they not up unto the heaven above them how We have made it and adorned it, no gaps are therein.\nوَالْاَرْضَ مَدَدْنٰهَا وَاَ لْقَيْنَا فِيْهَا رَوَاسِىَ وَاَنْۢبَتْنَا فِيْهَا مِنْ كُلِّ زَوْجٍۢ بَهِيْجٍ ۙ‏(7)\nWAL ARZA MADADNAAHAA WA LQAYNAA FEEHAA JA-A’LA WAANBATNAA FEEHAA MIN KULLE ZAWJIN BAHEEJIN.\nAnd the earth, We have spread it out, and have cast We therein mountains and have caused We therein the growth of all beauteous kinds,\nتَبْصِرَةً وَّذِكْرٰى لِكُلِّ عَبْدٍ مُّنِيْبٍ‏(8)\nTABSERATAN WA ZIKRAA LEKULLIM A’ABDIN MMUNEEBIN.\nTo serve insight and as a reminder unto every servant (of God) who turneth (unto His Lord).\nوَنَزَّلْنَا مِنَ السَّمَآءِ مَآءً مُّبٰرَكًا فَاَنْۢبَتْنَا بِهٖ جَنّٰتٍ وَّحَبَّ الْحَصِيْدِ ۙ‏(9)\nWA NAZZALNAA MENAL SAMAAA-E MAAA-AN MMUBAARAKAN FA-ANBATNAA BEHI JANNAATIN WWAHABBA AL-HASEEDE.\nAnd sent We down from the heaven water with blessings, and caused We to grow thereby gardens and the grain which is harvested,\nوَالنَّخْلَ بٰسِقٰتٍ لَّهَا طَلْعٌ نَّضِيْدٌ ۙ‏(10)\nWAALNNAKHLA BAASEQAATIN LLAHAA TALA’UN NNAZEEDUN.\nAnd the tall palm-trees with fruit-stalks, closely set one above another,\nرِّزْقًا لِّلْعِبَادِ‌ ۙ وَاَحْيَيْنَا بِهٖ بَلْدَةً مَّيْتًا‌ ؕ كَذٰلِكَ الْخُرُوْجُ‏(11)\nRIZQAN LLELE’EBAADE WAAHYAYNAA BEHI BALDATAN MMAYTAN KAZAALEKA AL-KHUROOJU.\nA sustenance for the servants, and give We life thereby unto a dead town; Thus will be the Resurrection.\nكَذَّبَتْ قَبْلَهُمْ قَوْمُ نُوْحٍ وَّاَصْحٰبُ الرَّسِّ وَثَمُوْدُۙ‏(12)\nKAZZABAT QABLAHUM QAWMO NOOHIN WWAASHAABU AR-RASSE WA SAMOODO.\nBelied (also) those before them the people of Noah and the dwellers of Ar-Rass and Thamood,\nوَعَادٌ وَّفِرْعَوْنُ وَاِخْوَانُ لُوْطٍۙ‏(13)\nWA A’ADUN WWAFERA’AWNU WAAKHWAANU LOOTIM.\nAnd ’Ad and Pharaoh, and the brethren of Lot,\nوَّاَصْحٰبُ الْاَيْكَةِ وَقَوْمُ تُبَّعٍ‌ؕ كُلٌّ كَذَّبَ الرُّسُلَ فَحَقَّ وَعِيْدِ‏(14)\nWWAASHAABU AL-AAYKATE WA QAWMO TUBBAA’IN KULLUL KAZZABA AR-RUSULA FA HAQQA WAE’EEDE.\nAnd the dwellers of the Wood and the people of Tubba; all belied the apostles, so was proved true My promise (of the doom).\nاَفَعَيِيْنَا بِالْخَلْقِ الْاَوَّلِ‌ؕ بَلْ هُمْ فِىْ لَبْسٍ مِّنْ خَلْقٍ جَدِيْدٍ‏(15)\nAAFAA’AYEENAA BIL-KHALQE AL-AAWLE BAL HUM FEE LABSIN MIN KHALQIN JADEEDIN.\nWhat! were We then wearied out with the first creation? Yet are they in doubt about the creation anew.\nوَلَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا الْاِنْسَانَ وَنَعْلَمُ مَا تُوَسْوِسُ بِهٖ نَفْسُهٗ ۖۚ وَنَحْنُ اَقْرَبُ اِلَيْهِ مِنْ حَبْلِ الْوَرِيْدِ‏(16)\nWA LAQAD KHALAQNAL INSAANA WA NA’LAMO MAA TOOSWESU BEHI NAFSUH WA NAHNO AQRABO ELAYHE MIN HABLE AL-WAREEDE.\nAnd indeed We created man, and know We whatever thoughts whispereth his self unto him, and We are nearer to him than his (very) life-vein.\nاِذْ يَتَلَقَّى الْمُتَلَقِّيٰنِ عَنِ الْيَمِيْنِ وَعَنِ الشِّمَالِ قَعِيْدٌ‏(17)\nIZ YATALAQQAA AL-MUTALAQQEENE A’NIL YAMEENE WA A’NIL SHEMAALE QAE’EEDUN.\nWhen receive (and record all doings) the two (guardian angels) appointed to receive, sitting, (one) on the right and (the other) on the left.\nمَا يَلْفِظُ مِنْ قَوْلٍ اِلَّا لَدَيْهِ رَقِيْبٌ عَتِيْدٌ‏(18)\nMAA YALFEZU MIN QAWLIN ILLAA LADAYHE RAQEEBUN A’ATEEDUN.\nHe pronounceth not a word but is unto him a watcher ready (to record)\nوَ جَآءَتْ سَكْرَةُ الْمَوْتِ بِالْحَقِّ‌ؕ ذٰلِكَ مَا كُنْتَ مِنْهُ تَحِيْدُ‏(19)\nWA JAAA-AT SAKRATU MAWT BIL-HAQ ZAALEKA MAA KUNTA MINHO TAHEEDU.\nAnd shall come the stupor of death in truth; that is (the state) which thou wast wont to shun.\nوَنُفِخَ فِى الصُّوْرِ ‌ؕ ذٰ لِكَ يَوْمُ الْوَعِيْدِ‏(20)\nWA FIL SOORE ZAA LEKA YAWMUD AL-WAE’EEDE.\nAnd shall be blown the Trumpet, it is the Day Promised (warned against).\nوَجَآءَتْ كُلُّ نَفْسٍ مَّعَهَا سَآئِقٌ وَّشَهِيْدٌ‏(21)\nWA JAAA-AT KULLO NAFSIM MMAA’AHAA SAAEQUN WWASHAHEEDUN.\nAnd shall come every soul, along with it a driver and a witness.\nلَقَدْ كُنْتَ فِىْ غَفْلَةٍ مِّنْ هٰذَا فَكَشَفْنَا عَنْكَ غِطَآءَكَ فَبَصَرُكَ الْيَوْمَ حَدِيْدٌ‏(22)\nLAQAD KUNTA FEE GHAFLATIM MIN HAAZAA FAKASHAFNAA A’NKAL GHETAAAKA FABASARUKA YAWMA HADEEDUN.\n(It will be said): “Thou wert heedless of this, now have We removed from thee thy veil, so thy sight today is sharp.\nوَقَالَ قَرِيْنُهٗ هٰذَا مَا لَدَىَّ عَتِيْدٌ ؕ‏(23)\nWA QAALA QAREENUH HAAZAA MAA LADAYYAL A’ATEEDUN.\nAnd shall say his companion: “This is what is ready with me\nاَلْقِيَا فِىْ جَهَنَّمَ كُلَّ كَفَّارٍ عَنِيْدٍۙ‏(24)\nAALQEEA FEE JAHANNAMA KULLA KAFFAARIN A’ANEEDIN.\n(It will be commanded): “Cast ye two into hell, every ingrate rebel,\nمَّنَّاعٍ لِّلْخَيْرِ مُعْتَدٍ مُّرِيْبِ ۙ‏(25)\nMMANNAAA’IN LLELKHAYRE MO’TADIN MMUREEBE.\nThe forbidder of good, the transgressor, the doubter,\nاۨلَّذِىْ جَعَلَ مَعَ اللّٰهِ اِلٰهًا اٰخَرَ فَاَ لْقِيٰهُ فِى الْعَذَابِ الشَّدِيْدِ‏(26)\nLAZEE JA-A’LA LAAHA LAAHE ELAAHANW AAKHAR FA-ALQEEHE LQEEHU FIL A’ZAABE ASH-SHADEEDE.\nWho did set up with God other gods, then cast him ye two into the severe chastisement.\nقَالَ قَرِيْنُهٗ رَبَّنَا مَاۤ اَطْغَيْتُهٗ وَلٰكِنْ كَانَ فِىْ ضَلٰلٍۢ بَعِيْدٍ‏(27)\nQAALA QAREENUH RABBANAA MAA AATGHAYTUH WA LAAKIL KAANA FEE ZALAALIM BA-E’ED.\nWill say his companion: “O’ Our Lord! I led him not to rebel but he had himself gone far astray\nقَالَ لَا تَخْتَصِمُوْا لَدَىَّ وَقَدْ قَدَّمْتُ اِلَيْكُمْ بِالْوَعِيْدِ‏(28)\nQAALA LAA TAKHTASEMOOA LADAYYAL WA QAD QADDAMTO ELAYKUM BIL-WAE’EEDE.\nHe shall say: “Wrangle ye not in my presence, Indeed I had sent beforehand unto you the warning:\nمَا يُبَدَّلُ الْقَوْلُ لَدَىَّ وَمَاۤ اَنَا بِظَلَّامٍ لِّلْعَبِيْدِ‏(29)\nMAA YUBADDALU QAWLO LADAYYAL WA MAA ANAA BEZALLAAMIL LIL-A’BEED.\nChangeth not the word with Me, nor am I (in the least) unjust unto (any of) the servants.\nيَوْمَ نَقُوْلُ لِجَهَنَّمَ هَلِ امْتَلَئْتِ وَتَقُوْلُ هَلْ مِنْ مَّزِيْدٍ‏(30)\nYAWMA NAQOOLU LE-JAHANNAMA HALE AMTALATE WA TAQOOLO HAL MIN MMAZEEDIN.\nThat day We will say unto hell: “Art thou filled up?” And it will say: “Are there (any) more?\nوَاُزْلِفَتِ الْجَنَّةُ لِلْمُتَّقِيْنَ غَيْرَ بَعِيْدٍ‏(31)\nWAAZLEFATE JANNATO LILMUTTAQEEN GHAYRA BA-E’ED.\nAnd the Garden (Paradise) shall be brought near unto the pious ones, not far (from thence).\nهٰذَا مَا تُوْعَدُوْنَ لِكُلِّ اَوَّابٍ حَفِيْظٍ‌ۚ‏(32)\nHAAZAA MAA TOO-A’DOON LEKULLIM AAWABIN HAFEEZIN.\nThis is what ye have been promised; (this is) for every one who turneth (frequently) unto God, (and) guardeth (His limits);\nمَنْ خَشِىَ الرَّحْمٰنَ بِالْغَيْبِ وَجَآءَ بِقَلْبٍ مُّنِيْبِۙ‏(33)\nMAN KHASHEAAA BIL-GHAYBE BIL-GHAYBE WA JAAA-A BEQALBIN MMUNEEBE.\nWho feareth the Beneficent God in secret, and cometh (unto Him) with a heart, turned (to Him in devotion)\nاۨدْخُلُوْهَا بِسَلٰمٍ‌ؕ ذٰلِكَ يَوْمُ الْخُلُوْدِ‏(34)\nADKHULOOHAA BESALAAMIN ZAALEKA YAWMUD AL-KHULOODE.\nEnter it ye in peace, this is the Day of eternal life!\nلَهُمْ مَّا يَشَآءُوْنَ فِيْهَا وَلَدَيْنَا مَزِيْدٌ‏(35)\nLAHUM MAA YASHAAOONA FEEHAA WA LADAYNAA MAZEEDUN.\nFor them therein shall be whatever they desire and with Us is yet more.\nوَكَمْ اَهْلَكْنَا قَبْلَهُمْ مِّنْ قَرْنٍ هُمْ اَشَدُّ مِنْهُمْ بَطْشًا فَنَقَّبُوْا فِى الْبِلَادِ ؕ هَلْ مِنْ مَّحِيْصٍ‏(36)\nWA AHLAKNAL QABLAHUM MIN QARNIN HUM ASHADDO MINHUM BATSHAN FANAQQABOOA FIL BELAADE HAL MIN MAHEES.\nAnd how many a generation We did destroy before them who were mightier than they in power! then they did wander through the lands; (searching) if there was any place of refuge (for them)?\nاِنَّ فِىْ ذٰلِكَ لَذِكْرٰى لِمَنْ كَانَ لَهٗ قَلْبٌ اَوْ اَلْقَى السَّمْعَ وَهُوَ شَهِيْدٌ‏(37)\nINNAL FEE ZAALEKA LAZEKRAA LEMAN-Y KAANA LAHU QALBUN AW AALQAA JA-A’LA WA HOWA WA.\nVerily in this is a reminder for him who hath a heart or he giveth ear with the presence of his mind.\nوَلَقَدْ خَلَقْنَا السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَ وَمَا بَيْنَهُمَا فِىْ سِتَّةِ اَيَّامٍ‌ۖ وَّمَا مَسَّنَا مِنْ لُّغُوْبٍ‏(38)\nWA LAQAD KHALAQNAL SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA WA MAA BAYNAHOMAA FEE SETTATE AYYAAMIN WA MAA MASSANAA MIN LLUGHOOBIN.\nAnd indeed created We the heavens and the earth and what is between them two, in six periods and touched Us not any fatigue.\nفَاصْبِرْ عَلٰى مَا يَقُوْلُوْنَ وَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ قَبْلَ طُلُوْعِ الشَّمْسِ وَقَبْلَ الْغُرُوْبِ‌ۚ‏(39)\nFAS-BIR A’LAA MAA YAQOOLOONA WASABBEH BE-HAMDE RABBEKA QABLA TULOOE’E ASH-SHAMSE WA QABLA AL-GHUROOBE.\nSo be thou patient on what they say, and celebrate the praise of thy Lord ere the rising of the sun and ere its setting,\nوَمِنَ الَّيْلِ فَسَبِّحْهُ وَاَدْبَارَ السُّجُوْدِ‏(40)\nWA MENAN LAYLE FASABBEHHU WAADBAARA SOJOOD.\nAnd in the night glorify Him and after the prostrations (prayers).\nوَاسْتَمِعْ يَوْمَ يُنَادِ الْمُنَادِ مِنْ مَّكَانٍ قَرِيْبٍۙ‏(41)\nWAASTAMEA’ YAWMA YUNAADE AL-MUNAADE MIN MAKAANIM QAREEBIN.\nAnd listen for the day whereon the crier shall cry from near place,\nيَوْمَ يَسْمَعُوْنَ الصَّيْحَةَ بِالْحَقِّ‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ يَوْمُ الْخُرُوْجِ‏(42)\nYAWMA YAS-MA-O’ONA AS-SAYHATA BIL-HAQQE ZAA LEKA YAWMUD AL-KHUROOJE.\nThe Day when they hear the cry in truth; that is the Day of coming forth (from the graves)\nاِنَّا نَحْنُ نُحْىٖ وَنُمِيْتُ وَاِلَيْنَا الْمَصِيْرُۙ‏(43)\nINNAA NAHNO NUHAA WANUMEETU WA ELAYNAA MASEER.\nVerily, We give life and cause death, and unto Us shall all return.\nيَوْمَ تَشَقَّقُ الْاَرْضُ عَنْهُمْ سِرَاعًا‌ ؕ ذٰ لِكَ حَشْرٌ عَلَيْنَا يَسِيْرٌ‏(44)\nYAWMA TASHAQQAQU ARZO A’NHUM SERAAA’AN ZAA LEKA HASHRUN A’LAYNAA YASEERUN.\nThe Day on which the earth shall cleave asunder under them, they will make haste; that is a gathering together easy for Us,\nنَحْنُ اَعْلَمُ بِمَا يَقُوْلُوْنَ‌ وَمَاۤ اَنْتَ عَلَيْهِمْ بِجَبَّارٍ‌ فَذَكِّرْ بِالْقُرْاٰنِ مَنْ يَّخَافُ وَعِيْدِ‏(45)\nNAHNO A-A’LAMO BEMAA YAQOOLOONA WA MAA ANTA A’LAYHIM BEJABBAARIN FA-ZAKKIR BE-QUR-AANE MAN YYAKHAAFU WAE’EEDE.\nWe know best what they say, and thou art not one to compel them; therefore remind him though the Quran who feareth My threat.",
  "merits": "Surah Qaaf\nThis Surah is ‘Makki’ and it has 45 verses. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) has said that whoever recites this Surah frequently will not suffer at the time of death. Reciting Surah Qaaf in salaat increases one’s sustenance and makes the accounting of the Day of Judgement easy.\nWriting and drinking water in which this Surah has been dissolved cures one of many acute diseases. Verse 23 of this Surah is especially good for the cure of eye ailments. One can recite this verse and blow into some water and then drink it, and by the will of Allah (s.w.t.) any problem with eyes will be cured."
}
